   "evidence": "Line 55 has `@[simp] theorem hammingNorm_indicator_one`. Line 66 has `theorem hammingDist_indicator_one [DecidableEq \u03b9] (s t : Finset \u03b9) : hammingDist (...indicator 1) (...indicator 1) = (s \u2206 t).card` with no attribute. Its only use, in SparsePacking.lean:74, is an explicit `rw [hammingDist_indicator_one]`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/InformationTheory/Hamming.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp]` to `hammingDist_indicator_one`. Its right side, `(s \u2206 t).card`, is already simp-normal and does not mention indicators, so the rewrite cannot loop.",
   "issue": "`Finset.hammingDist_indicator_one` rewrites `hammingDist` of two finset indicators to `(s \u2206 t).card`. That is the same normal-form lemma as `hammingNorm_indicator_one` (line 55, tagged `@[simp]`), but this one has no `@[simp]`. As a result, `simp` reduces indicator weights but not indicator distances, and consumers must call the lemma by name with `rw`.",
